WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:15.840
What’s so important about a dinner scene? And why would a director waste their time on something

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.339
so simple? That’s what we’re going to
focus on today, so welcome, to Now You See I-

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.160
I think dinner scenes are some of the most
powerful and revealing scenes in film. They

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.020
always show much more than people eating. They show communion. When I say communion, I mean an

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.830
act of sharing and peace between the people
at the dinner table. Directors use the dinner

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.250
scene to show us relationships between each
character. How they get along, or how they don't.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.540
But I think even more is going on.
We all know the process of eating a typical

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.239
dinner. You eat, talk about your day, make
a few jokes, and call it a night. So when

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:08.810
a meal goes wrong in a film, we especially
notice because we’re used to dinners going

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:15.710
a certain way. And that’s what gives a dinner
scene so much potential, either for humor,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.479
or for drama.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.700
Let's look at what dinner scenes can accomplish in three sections: Humans Eat, the Conflict, and The Unexpected

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:46.140
Whether you’re a  contract killer or a demi-God, you have to eat. And that makes you human.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.619
Showing characters eating makes them human, like us. It puts us into their world. It makes us relate with

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:57.399
them. We can’t relate to stealing diamonds
or getting shot, but we can relate to getting

00:01:57.399 --> 00:02:01.179
in an argument at the table. Dinner scenes
make us empathize with characters. Tarantino

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:04.729
uses the dinner scene very well in Reservoir
Dogs and Pulp Fiction to pull us into the

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:08.259
world of his films. When these characters,
who we just saw have a friendly meal, start

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.819
getting shot and rob the restaurant, it’s
that much more shocking because we saw them

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.339
as who they were, people. People who eat just
like we do.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.379
When people come together for dinner, it’s
supposed to be a peaceful communion. But it

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:22.790
doesn’t always go that way. Dinner scenes
are perfect ways to show conflict. When people

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.690
storm out

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.400
break dishes

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.400
or get left alone

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.640
that says a lot about the characters without having to tell us.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.200
And so a successful meal means just the opposite.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.370
Dinner doesn’t always go smoothly. It doesn’t
for us in real life, and it certainly doesn’t

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.799
for the characters in a movie. Since we can
relate to how awkward a meal can be, it can

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:01.559
be that much funnier when a dinner scene doesn’t
go as expected.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.500
Or it can be that much more dramatic.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.840
To go from the familiar dinner scene to an
alien busting out of somebodies’ chest really

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.080
adds to the horror.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.260
A dinner that’s just a dinner would be boring.
A director wouldn’t waste a scene with something

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.219
as simple as people eating if it wasn’t
to show something more important. That’s

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:39.510
what I love about film. A film doesn’t have
to tell us something. It doesn’t have to

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.090
tell us “this person doesn’t get along
this person” or “this person is human

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.150
just like you.” It can show us.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.940
Showing rather than telling is what makes a film go from good to great.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.940
And a dinner scene can
be quite the show.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.350
Thanks for Watching

